"""qbench — the quasar-bench agent CLI.

Stdlib only (Python 3.9+). It imports `bench.py` from the same directory, so
the pair can be vendored together; `make qbench` also builds a single-file
zipapp, and a running bench serves one at /cli/qbench.

Setup, once:

    curl -fsSL "$BENCH_URL/install.sh" | sh     # BENCH_URL = your bench server
    install -m 600 /dev/null ~/.config/qbench/key   # then put the key in it
    qbench doctor

Server: BENCH_URL, else ~/.config/qbench/url (the installer writes it). There
is deliberately no built-in default, so no server name ships inside a copy of
this file that gets vendored into a public repo. The key comes from BENCH_KEY, else
~/.config/qbench/key (must be chmod 600). The key is never printed.

The commands most agents need:

    qbench check                       # did HEAD regress vs. the last benched commit?
    qbench sprint put --repo accreleus/quasar --sprint c15 --title … --sections s.json
    qbench sprint status --repo accreleus/quasar --sprint c15
    qbench run new --suite abr-ladder --scenario 1080p120 --repo accreleus/quasar --commit "$SHA"
    qbench evidence gaps

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 2 usage, 3 check found a regression,
4 check had nothing comparable, 5 key missing/unreadable/rejected.
Every command takes --json; see docs/design/2026-09-22-c15-agent-skills-spec.md.
